id: 1114
event: stage_changed
data: {"id":1114,"ts":"2026-10-23T23:20:57.948236+00:00","type":"stage_changed","payload":{"stage":"OPTIMIZE","goal":"Improve the measured design. Compare at least one variant even if initial timing passes. Prefer meeting the requested frequency and WNS>=0, then lower stdcell area, then lower flow-reported power. You may propose up to three run_flow calls in one pure-flow batch. Never mix flow calls with writes/tests in the same response. RTL changes must re-pass the existing VERIFY tests before any flow. Record the rationale for each variant.","previous_ok":true,"design_spec":{"top_module":"uart_tx","summary":"UART transmitter with 8N1 framing, LSB-first data, idle-high serial output, and a configurable integer baud divider.","ports":[{"name":"clk","direction":"input","width":1,"description":"Clock; all sequential behavior occurs on rising edges."},{"name":"rst_n","direction":"input","width":1,"description":"Synchronous active-low reset."},{"name":"data_in","direction":"input","width":8,"description":"Byte captured when a start request is accepted."},{"name":"start","direction":"input","width":1,"description":"Level-sensitive transmit request, accepted only while idle."},{"name":"tx","direction":"output","width":1,"description":"Serial output, high while idle and during the stop bit."},{"name":"busy","direction":"output","width":1,"description":"High throughout transmission, including the full stop bit."}],"behavior":["1. Provide integer parameter BAUD_DIV with default 16; supported values are integers greater than or equal to 1. Each transmitted bit lasts exactly BAUD_DIV clock periods.","2. On any rising clock edge with rst_n low, reset takes priority over start, sets tx high and busy low, and discards any active transmission. Reset has no effect between rising clock edges.","3. On a rising edge with rst_n high, busy low, and start high, capture data_in, assert busy, and drive tx low to begin the start bit immediately after that edge.","4. Each frame consists of one low start bit, eight captured data bits transmitted least significant bit first, and one high stop bit. No parity bit is transmitted.","5. For a frame accepted at edge E, transmit the start bit for BAUD_DIV periods, then each data bit for BAUD_DIV periods, then the stop bit for BAUD_DIV periods. Deassert busy at edge E + 10*BAUD_DIV and keep tx high.","6. Ignore start and changes to data_in while busy is high before a rising edge, including the edge that completes the stop bit. Requests are not queued.","7. When idle without an accepted request, keep tx high and busy low. If start remains high, accept another frame on the first rising edge after busy has deasserted, capturing the data_in value at that edge."],"targets":{"clock_mhz":50.0,"max_area_um2":null,"fit":"tt_1x1_tile"},"test_plan":["Verify synchronous reset from idle and during a frame: asserting rst_n between rising edges has no immediate effect; the next rising edge sets tx high and busy low. Confirm reset overrides start and no discarded frame resumes.","Transmit 0xA5 with BAUD_DIV=4 and check every clock period of the start bit, all eight LSB-first data bits, the stop bit, and exact busy duration.","Transmit 0x00 and 0xFF and verify framing, idle-high behavior before and after frames, and full stop-bit duration.","Change data_in and pulse start during an active frame, including its completion edge; verify the captured byte is unchanged and no request is queued.","Hold start high across frame completion and verify a new frame begins exactly one clock edge after busy deasserts, using the newly sampled data_in.","Repeat framing and exact timing checks with BAUD_DIV=1 and BAUD_DIV=3 to exercise minimum-divider and non-power-of-two counter boundaries."],"purely_combinational":false}}}

